## Why a marker and not a disabled workflow

A disabled workflow only stops its *schedule*. On 2026-11-21 a manual dispatch, a
re-run of an old job, a local `python3 ops/bank_publish.py` and an agent session
would all have kept posting. `ops/HOLD.md` was documentation only — nothing read
it. This file is read by code, so "the hold is on" is a fact the uploader checks,
not a note a human is trusted to remember.

